== multi-band variant: internal bands exactly flat at energy M (no group velocity, no stress) ==
contribution per internal mode: rho = M/2, p = 0, mu = 0 (any completion), <E_x - H> = -M/2, A = -1 per quantum.
M=1.0, L=8: internal fraction 0.998047; rho+p from internal = 0.4990 per fine site (does not fall)
M=1.0, L=64: internal fraction 0.999996; rho+p from internal = 0.5000 per fine site (does not fall)
M=1.0, L=1024: internal fraction 1.000000; rho+p from internal = 0.5000 per fine site (does not fall)
M=2.0, L=8: internal fraction 0.998047; rho+p from internal = 0.9980 per fine site (does not fall)
M=2.0, L=64: internal fraction 0.999996; rho+p from internal = 1.0000 per fine site (does not fall)
M=2.0, L=1024: internal fraction 1.000000; rho+p from internal = 1.0000 per fine site (does not fall)

== Bose-Fermi paired variant (one complex boson + one two-band fermion with |eps| = omega, same flow coupling) ==
vacuum energy E0_B(h) + E0_F(h) = sum_k omega_h(k) - sum_k omega_h(k) = 0 for every h and every design: rho, p, a_x, mu all cancel
mode by mode (construction-level identity). The operator anomaly sum_k (u_xx-1) eps_k n_k on real quanta has the same sign
for both statistics and does NOT cancel.
